# Load-bearing, not hygiene. If a host copy of a generated package leaks into
# the build context it is not necessarily overwritten by regeneration — stale
# extra files survive — and the image silently ships a different contract from
# spec/openapi.yaml. The `generated` stage asserts the first two paths are
# absent; the `build` stage asserts the third path's CONTENT IS UNCHANGED by
# its COPYs (that path already legitimately exists before the build stage's
# COPYs run, so an absence check can't apply there — see the Dockerfile's
# `build`-stage comments). This file is what makes both assertions pass.
packages/types/src
packages/client/src
apps/api/src/generated

# Host build output and dependencies. Copying these in would defeat layer
# caching, mix Windows-built artefacts into a Linux image, and — for
# node_modules — bring native binaries built for the wrong platform.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Never in an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Irrelevant to a build; excluded to keep the context small and the cache stable.
.git
.github
.superpowers
docs
tests
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.playwright
*.md
!README.md
